 Onboarding strategy — chosen: hybrid (1-field UI + chat)

 Why this and not pure in-chat or full wizard: Pure in-chat is lazy — Turtle only learns names when users volunteer them, which can take many turns; strangers won't know they need to. A full signup wizard is friction theater — most
 users bounce before turn 1. The hybrid gives Turtle a name to use immediately, then lets the existing extraction + confirmation gate pipeline naturally fill in the rest (city, role, preferences, contacts) over the first dozen
 turns. This is the right balance: 30 seconds of UI, then the memory architecture does its job.

 Flow:
 1. New browser hits /. Server checks for turtle_uid cookie. None → renders the onboarding screen (not the chat).
 2. Onboarding screen: email field (required, for magic link) + name field (required) + timezone (auto-detected from browser, hidden). One button: "Send me a link to start".
 3. Server: creates pending user in IdentityManager, sends magic-link email containing a signed token. No password.
 4. User clicks link → backend verifies token, sets turtle_uid cookie (HTTP-only, signed), resolves to canonical user_id, writes seed facts directly to identity.md via the memory pipeline (source=explicit, applied=True, bypassing
 the confirmation gate since the user typed them in a form). Redirects to chat.
 5. First chat turn: Turtle's prompt template detects the just-populated identity block and greets: "Nice to meet you, {Name}. What would you like to start with?"
 6. From here on, normal flow. The confirmation gate handles every other fact extraction passively as the conversation unfolds.

 Returning user: Cookie present → resolves to existing user_id → straight into chat. No re-auth unless cookie expires (suggest 90 days). If cookie is missing on a different device, they can re-request the magic link with the same
 email; IdentityManager resolves the same user_id.

 Memory architecture changes required for this: none structural. Existing schema accepts the form-submitted facts as MemoryEvent with source=explicit, applied=True. The pipeline already supports this path.

