 ---
 What's deliberately NOT in this plan

 - Multi-device sync via mobile app — magic-link auth on a different browser is enough for V1. Native apps come later.
 - Real OAuth (Google/Apple) — magic link is enough friction-wise; OAuth adds vendor lock-in and isn't necessary until you have a reason.
 - Encrypted-at-rest memory — defer until you have data sensitive enough to need it. Adds key management complexity.
 - Channel adapter rollout (WhatsApp/iMessage/Slack/Twilio) — already deferred per project memory. These work today on the user_id layer; they just need the same web-cookie/magic-link bridge so a phone number can be linked to an
 existing web user.
 - A "merge two accounts" flow — when a user signs up via magic link then later links WhatsApp, they'll get two user_ids. Build merge UI when this actually happens to someone, not preemptively.

